BigDataflow is publicly available: https://github.com/BigDataflow-
system . All the experimental data can be accessed via the link: https:
//figshare.com/articles/dataset/material_fse23_zip/21971945/3 .

The replication package is available at https://github.com/XJTU-NetVerify/accessrefinery/ and is
archived on Zenodo [ 36 ]. We cannot release the real-world datasets due to customer permissions,
as they contain confidential information. The replication package includes:
• The implementation of AccessRefinery ;
• The reproduced implementation of Access Analyzer ;
• Scripts for invoking Access Analyzer via AWS Command-Line Interface (CLI);
• Two synthetic datasets derived from real-world cases.
Proc. ACM Softw. Eng., Vol. 3, No. FSE, Article FSE059. Publication date: July 2026.
AccessRefinery: Fast Mining Concise Access Control Intents on Public Cloud FSE059:21

The source code of PoCGen , the new dataset, and all experiment scripts are available at https:
//github.com/sola-st/PoCGen, and also as a permanent snapshot at https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.
19550952.
